</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intraocular concentration and pharmacokinetics of triamcinolone acetonide after a single intravitreal injection.</article-title><source>Ophthalmology</source><year>2003</year><volume>110</volume><fpage>681</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12689886</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tan</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Peters</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaufman</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Recent developments in understanding the pathophysiology of elevated intraocular pressure.</article-title><source>Curr Opin Ophthalmol</source><year>2006</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>168</fpage><lpage>74</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16552252</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>R</given-names><suffix>III</suffix></name><name><surname>Rhee</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Corticosteroid-induced ocular hypertension and glaucoma: a brief review and update of the literature.</article-title><source>Curr Opin Ophthalmol</source><year>2006</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>163</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16552251</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yeung</surname><given-names>CK</given-names></name><name><surname>Chan</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name><name><surname>Chiang</surname><given-names>SW</given-names></name><name><surname>Pang</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Lam</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name></person-group><artic